scope: |
  ScalaScript 3 — a new module built around SSC IR: a linear, register-based instruction
  sequence with WebAssembly-style structured control flow, replacing v2's recursively-walked
  term tree. Zero external dependencies in the kernel, enforced at the Prim boundary; the
  kernel written in the Scala 3 ∩ ScalaScript 2 subset so self-hosting is a consequence and
  the two hosts give a byte-identical differential gate.
  Design: v3/specs/10-ssc-ir.md. Queue: v3/SPRINT.md.
  Touches outside v3/: one row in tests/fixtures/modules.tsv (module registration), and two
  BUGS entries filed where their fixes go — root (new-array-n-builds-a-one-element-array,
  lane multi) and scripts/ (coord-claim-broad-reason-lands-inside-the-paths-field). Boards
  are shared at every level and exempt from claims (P-2.3).
